# Browser control: chrome-cli first

Owner preference (2026-09-01): drive the user's real Chrome with `chrome-cli`
(`/opt/homebrew/bin/chrome-cli`) whenever it can do the job — list, open,
close and activate tabs and windows, navigate, reload, read a page
(`source`), run JavaScript in a tab (`execute`), window size and position.
One Bash call, no MCP session to stand up.

Use the chrome-devtools MCP only for what chrome-cli cannot do: DOM
snapshots and element interaction (click, fill, hover), network request
inspection, console messages, screenshots, performance traces, and dialog
handling. Starting a devtools session for something `chrome-cli list tabs`
or `chrome-cli source` answers is the mistake this rule exists to prevent.
